# BEGIN odile-releases
# /releases/* — the tenant image the Servury panel downloads (ODL-332).
#
# The panel's Boot image and Disk image fields take an https URL plus a
# SHA-256; the node downloads the file, checks the declared hash and re-hashes
# it at every start. Caddy streams the file: no application in the path, Range
# and large bodies are Caddy's, and the stdlib app server never holds 3 GB in
# memory. The directory is /srv/odile-releases (outside the repo: the
# image is a build artefact, named by its hash in the panel and in
# docs/evidence/m1-tenant.md, never committed).
#
# handle_path strips /releases, so /releases/m1/odile-tenant.efi is the file
# /srv/odile-releases/m1/odile-tenant.efi. `no-store`: the URL is stable
# per card but the bytes change when an image is rebuilt, and a cached copy
# would fail the panel's hash check in a way nobody can see.
#
# This block must stay before the site's catch-all `handle` (it is: the seed
# block it sits beside is spliced after it). A change here needs
# `systemctl restart caddy` — Caddy runs with `admin off`.
handle_path /releases/* {
	root * /srv/odile-releases
	header Cache-Control "no-store"
	file_server
}
# END odile-releases
